      "message": "IPC ISR is sending one of the following two events \n- WAKE EVENT if there\u0027s a task blocked in ipc_read(..., -1).\n- EVENT_FLAG_BIT_HECI_MSG if user specified. Which means user wants to handle the event. this is for a task waiting for other events at the same time. Still although user specified event while ipc_open(), if there\u0027s any blocking ipc_read(..., -1) call, then IPC ISR only send WAKE EVENT to the task blocked in ipc_read().\n\nFor short, if user called ipc_open(..., 0) with no event specified, then there\u0027s no event visible to user. In this case, IPC ISR only sends the event when there\u0027s a task blocked in ipc_read(). \n\nAnyway, this will be gone, since I\u0027ll go back to old IPC implementation.",
